                        </section>
                        <section class="s_text_block_split pb80 o_colored_level o_cc o_cc5 pt56" data-snippet="s_text_block_split" data-name="Text Split" id="We-didn't-open-our-doors-just-to-sell-bikes.-We-opened-them-to-share-a-passion-for-freedom%2C-fresh-air%2C-and-the-simple-joy-of-the-open-road." data-anchor="true">
                            <div class="container" data-lt-tmp-id="lt-366726" data-gramm="false" spellcheck="false" data-lpop-hide-native-caret="">
                                <div class="row">
                                    <div class="o_colored_level col-lg-5">
                                        <p class="small"><strong>OUR STORY</strong></p>
                                        <p><span class="h4-fs"><strong>We didn't open our doors just to sell bikes. We opened them to share a passion for freedom, fresh air, and the simple joy of the open road.<br/><br/></strong></span></p>
                                        <p><span class="h4-fs"><strong><a href="/contactus" class="o_translate_inline btn btn-secondary"><span class="h6-fs">Contact us&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; <span class="fa fa-angle-right"/></span></a>&amp;nbsp;</strong></span></p>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="o_colored_level pt40 offset-lg-1 col-lg-6">
                                        <p>That's why our team isn't just here to make a sale. Every person behind our counter and in our workshop is a rider first, someone who knows what it feels like to test a new set of tires on a wet cobblestone street, or to nurse an old frame back to life instead of replacing it. We ask questions before we recommend a product, because the right bike for a daily commute through Brussels traffic is rarely the right bike for weekend rides through the Ardennes. We're here to build a community of riders who trust us with their gear and their goals, so that every visit feels less like a transaction and more like coming home.</p><p>Founded right here in Brussels, Off Track&amp;nbsp;started as a small workshop with a handful of tools and a lot of stubbornness. Word got around, the workshop got busier, and eventually we opened our doors as a full shop: bikes, accessories, fittings, repairs, all under one roof. Today we sell online as well, but our heart never left the workshop floor. Whatever you buy from us, online or in person, it's backed by a team you can actually walk in and talk to, on a street you can actually find us on.</p>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </section>
